%N A401478 Numbers that are not the sum of at most seven 6-full numbers.
%C A401478 Erdős and Ivić conjectured that every sufficiently large integer is the sum of at most r+1 r-full numbers; for r = 6 this would imply that this sequence is finite.
%C A401478 The last known term is a(37036) = 4034495. There are no other terms below 10^10.
%H A401478 Leandre Jack, <a href="/A401478/b401478.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..37036</a>
%H A401478 Thomas Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/1107">Problem #1107</a>, Erdős Problems.
%H A401478 Leandre Jack, <a href="https://github.com/leandrejack-afk/erdos-computations/blob/main/e1107/README.md">Erdős Problem 1107: numbers that are not a sum of at most r + 1 r-full numbers</a>, GitHub.
%Y A401478 Cf. A056828 (r=2), A392342 (r=3), A392343 (r=4), A401477 (r=5).
